# PrivacyWeave — Inbound Opportunity

---

## What They Do

PrivacyWeave is an early-stage startup building a runtime data usage control plane — a mandatory enforcement layer that sits between any system and its data destination, evaluating every sensitive data access in real time before the data moves. It is positioned not as DLP, not as a data catalogue, and not as IAM — but as the missing primitive between policy documents and actual enforcement.

The core value proposition: governance fails because data usage is never evaluated at the moment it matters. Everything today is either defined in advance (policies) or reconstructed later (logs). PrivacyWeave inserts a mandatory decision point — evaluate who is accessing, why, where it is going, and which fields are sensitive — and returns one authoritative decision (allow / partial mask / deny) in under 100ms, with an automatic audit log written for every decision.

**Go-to-market wedge:** CRM contact exports — high-risk, universal, almost never logged. Target: Series A-C B2B SaaS companies preparing for SOC2 or enterprise deals.

**India relevance:** DPDP Act 2023 makes this product directly relevant to Indian data fiduciaries. The "purpose limitation" requirement (data collected for one purpose cannot be quietly reused to train a model) maps precisely to PrivacyWeave's runtime purpose-check architecture. DPDP breach notification timelines also create urgency for audit-trail infrastructure.

